			'The Greek is praus (noun prautēs), used of strength under control, like a strong horse trained to the bridle. The Hebrew behind Matthew 5:5 is anav, the humble person who depends on our Father; Psalm 37:11, which Jesus quotes, reads in the FHB, “But the humble will inherit the land.”',
	},
	{
		question: 'Does meek mean weak?',
