			'No. Scripture calls Moses “very humble, more than anyone else on the face of the earth” (Numbers 12:3), using the same Hebrew word, and Jesus calls Himself “gentle and humble in heart” (Matthew 11:29). Meekness is power that serves rather than dominates.',
	},
	{
		question: 'What does “the meek shall inherit the earth” mean?',
		answer:
			'It means our Father gives the earth to His humble, trusting children rather than to those who seize it. Jesus draws the promise from Psalm 37:11, and an inheritance is something a father gives his children, not something they win by force.',
	},
];
